# ARCDevTools — Pinned Quality Tool Versions
#
# SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the SwiftLint / SwiftFormat versions used by
# ARC Labs Studio. Every consumer of these tools resolves the version here:
#
#   - CI workflows          (workflows-spm/quality.yml, workflows-ios/quality.yml)
#   - Xcode Cloud           (templates/ci_scripts/ci_post_clone.sh)
#   - Git hooks             (hooks/pre-commit, hooks/pre-push)
#   - Local scripts / make  (scripts/lint.sh, scripts/format.sh, scripts/pr-ready.sh)
#
# `arcdevtools-setup` copies this file into every consumer project as
# `.arc-tool-versions` (studio-owned, refreshed on every run).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# Before pinning, three different SwiftLint versions were in play at once:
# dev machines (whatever brew installed months ago), SPM CI (`brew install
# swiftlint` = always latest), and iOS CI (a moving Docker tag behind
# norio-nomura/action-swiftlint). Rules change between releases, so a PR that
# was green locally failed in CI — most visibly with
# `superfluous_disable_command` errors under `--strict`, where an older
# SwiftLint required a disable comment that a newer one no longer needs.
#
# HOW TO BUMP
# -----------
# 1. Change a version below.
# 2. Run `./ARCDevTools/scripts/install-tools.sh` locally, then `make lint format`.
# 3. Fix any new violations, commit, tag a release.
# 4. Consumer projects pick it up on their next submodule update + setup run.
#
# Releases:
#   SwiftLint   https://github.com/realm/SwiftLint/releases
#   SwiftFormat https://github.com/nicklockwood/SwiftFormat/releases

SWIFTLINT_VERSION=0.65.0
SWIFTFORMAT_VERSION=0.62.1
